# Line endings — LF everywhere, on every machine.
#
# Not a style preference: this project *enforces* LF (`.editorconfig` sets
# `end_of_line = lf`, Prettier sets `endOfLine: "lf"`). Git on Windows defaults
# to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout — so without
# this file a fresh clone on Windows fails `npm run verify` at the very first
# step, format:check, on code nobody touched.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` overrides any contributor's local `core.autocrlf`, so the
# working copy matches what the repo stores and what CI checks.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary

# Generated. Collapsed in PR diffs, and excluded from language stats so the
# repo is not reported as mostly JSON.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
